cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use voice2brain in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "voice2brain: voice notes into a linked markdown knowledge base"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/voice2brain"
url: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/voice2brain"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - speech to text
  - personal knowledge management
  - second brain
  - Whisper
  - markdown
abstract: >-
  A primitive rather than a platform: four small Python scripts that take any audio
  file and produce linked, tagged, searchable markdown. Transcription wraps Whisper
  with defaults tuned on messy phone-mic recordings; ingestion adds frontmatter,
  frequency-based tags with no LLM call, wiki-links derived from title-word overlap,
  an optional summary and an optional vector index. Plain files are the database and
  SQLite is only a derived index; every optional dependency degrades along a ladder
  rather than failing.
